(e) So far as the animals are concerned, life means something more than mere survival or existence or instrumental value for human beings, but to lead a life with some intrinsic worth, honour and dignity;

(f) Right to live in a healthy and clean atmosphere and right to get protection from human beings against inflicting unnecessary pain or suffering is a right guaranteed to the animals under Sections 3 and 11 of the PCA Act read with Clause (g) of Article 51A of the Constitution of India;
(g) Right to dignity and fair treatment is not confined to human beings alone, but it applies to animals as well;
(h) Right not to be beaten, kicked or overriden is also a right recognized by Sections 3 and 11 of the PCA Act;
